{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voices": [
    "en-US-AndrewNeural"
  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "17",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p17-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f",
        "2": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174",
        "3": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s01-c1-145e8bc78843",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Two healthy A P I tasks are already serving requests. Before changing anything, pin the trusted image and confirm the task definition, role and network settings. The new tasks must be able to start and receive the same health checks.",
          "text_sha256": "145e8bc7884306272965ef023d8eaf1bc42647d258af838bfad9546443628519",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cfa7d84ed02dea1b8d9f5e835d081ae4a8e17f724921f7c48406143e90d488fa",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s01-c2-d734e3a498fe",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Deploy the service in the sandbox and check running tasks, target health and a real test request. This gives you a known healthy baseline before the new revision arrives.",
          "text_sha256": "d734e3a498fe2faa761ce79211619ce3f17f0a6c6ba7fd67f1a78c77dc828a56",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d734e3a498fe2faa761ce79211619ce3f17f0a6c6ba7fd67f1a78c77dc828a56",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s01-c3-30224a442777",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Deploy the new revision and inspect its replacement tasks. A started task isn't enough; verify app and target health before letting healthy old tasks retire.",
          "text_sha256": "30224a44277710cd401c825d479dd0ec50dfcd3df0b112be401deb3a12d444ca",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "30224a44277710cd401c825d479dd0ec50dfcd3df0b112be401deb3a12d444ca",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s01-c4-ad3e2f0e50b3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For the sandbox drill, simulate a failed health response and compare task events and target health. Observe the configured recovery or rollback. Remove the test resources once you've verified it.",
          "text_sha256": "ad3e2f0e50b3687533efea06c58308f5f15789486888d97e3854e2c198ee8444",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ad3e2f0e50b3687533efea06c58308f5f15789486888d97e3854e2c198ee8444",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s02-c1-9f5ee46b25c1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Push an approved test image to the private repository. Record the returned digest. That identifies the actual artifact even if a tag can move.",
          "text_sha256": "9f5ee46b25c115bf2fdd21588093249704bb8216d53966f3c9873c4b4e297a0e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9f5ee46b25c115bf2fdd21588093249704bb8216d53966f3c9873c4b4e297a0e",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s02-c2-e85490637282",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Inspect findings for that exact digest and confirm that the intended caller can pull the image. Evaluate tag immutability separately rather than treating a good scan as proof of access.",
          "text_sha256": "e8549063728294a6a2e2e2f67fcd8fbe05ff7ba12e837b106f72013c0842e671",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e8549063728294a6a2e2e2f67fcd8fbe05ff7ba12e837b106f72013c0842e671",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s02-c3-dfd39b029267",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Preview the lifecycle rule and verify the known-good rollback digest stays available. Test a pull of the image you would actually need to restore.",
          "text_sha256": "dfd39b0292674359b48c6e9b060be906f4cf8fb05a770a82c6133da33783016b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "dfd39b0292674359b48c6e9b060be906f4cf8fb05a770a82c6133da33783016b",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s02-c4-13579c36aeda",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If testing replication, compare the destination digest with the source. The image arriving proves registry replication, not that the app can deploy in the second Region.",
          "text_sha256": "13579c36aeda16b34a268fff48924ac631d0325edf6be5da3bd1142e60a5e868",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "13579c36aeda16b34a268fff48924ac631d0325edf6be5da3bd1142e60a5e868",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s03-c1-d58696c05228",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A Pod is Pending. Before raising capacity, check its events and the scheduling reason. The sandbox example makes the resource request larger than what eligible nodes can supply.",
          "text_sha256": "d58696c05228f257c49e563de06b9b96e97798bc08f025a674a2530294dfb680",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d58696c05228f257c49e563de06b9b96e97798bc08f025a674a2530294dfb680",
          "asset_sha256": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s03-c2-55f9eec30ac5",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If the event says insufficient C P U, compare the Pod's requested resources with the eligible nodes. Reduce an excessive request or add compatible capacity. A failed image pull would need a different fix.",
          "text_sha256": "55f9eec30ac589f00c07bcd2d987f023aeea127aac185ea84f953cde68e774f1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "349acf506035e0126f854dbf64ce8d7aadf6ea6f9672c7c4ecb14b78a9177eb1",
          "asset_sha256": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-andrew-exp-s03-c3-8eac565f67b7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Wait for the Pod to become Ready, then send a request through the Service. Removing the Pending status isn't enough to prove the app is reachable.",
          "text_sha256": "8eac565f67b75ab68396da91363e9056c496d38db9b4e6841546361e058dd561",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8eac565f67b75ab68396da91363e9056c496d38db9b4e6841546361e058dd561",
          "asset_sha256": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "18",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m12p18-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p18-andrew-exp-s01-c1-5bf9a145c769",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use two otherwise similar test requests. Tenant A should reach its own service data. The same caller should be denied for Tenant B's data. A successful login only answers who the caller is.",
          "text_sha256": "5bf9a145c769971911ed31c2364f2f003a788ae89346ada8bb967ce4a10c09be",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5bf9a145c769971911ed31c2364f2f003a788ae89346ada8bb967ce4a10c09be",
          "asset_sha256": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p18-andrew-exp-s01-c2-9ea42771539c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check the application authorization, workload I A M and enforcing network policy separately. A denied network request does not by itself prove that the data layer rejects the wrong tenant.",
          "text_sha256": "9ea42771539cac847e35f5abb674a3f34238e0a2448304b17cc18a256099311e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2b5e50911848ae4fae761a8db4675d15ca318aa83e9254210c6d485e2f62c3d2",
          "asset_sha256": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p18-andrew-exp-s01-c3-d4161f658c06",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check logs and policy evidence for the actual decision, then verify that no cross-tenant record was returned. Save the test result and remove the sandbox resources.",
          "text_sha256": "d4161f658c0649ff708a7b8a3573b2224016e262d7af5e6feea0b1802c43b955",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d4161f658c0649ff708a7b8a3573b2224016e262d7af5e6feea0b1802c43b955",
          "asset_sha256": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "13",
      "part": "01",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m13p01-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "eda09f8926c869c8e1a51c9966a87464b23fec963dc4c10abc9c5f7f5889298b",
        "2": "cbfaea8e44f86bbce0b092072c0aa39005b4162fe3aa00f38fae903cab554ed7",
        "3": "ae29b7d495392cb8921f3d7846ad319e4eb7409410eac0ea370b4505e13c58e0"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s01-c1-79dcce571227",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "An image arrives in S three. An object-created event invokes Lambda to make the thumbnail, and the function writes the result to a separate destination. The upload and thumbnail work don't have to happen on one server.",
          "text_sha256": "79dcce57122789c59d757e7d5155d88d39306db380bc6efe7d067fd944c0f552",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "98425650adeef6e633647145721d9c9deb41fdb830843a7dca40ca30c581e65a",
          "asset_sha256": "eda09f8926c869c8e1a51c9966a87464b23fec963dc4c10abc9c5f7f5889298b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s01-c2-97044a25e4a0",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A later invocation might reuse a warm environment, but it does not have to. Keep the thumbnail in durable storage and make a repeated event safe to handle.",
          "text_sha256": "97044a25e4a0440cbdc5c6fd7d040aa5966e9cb78b4f93a849df99a5b250efd2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "97044a25e4a0440cbdc5c6fd7d040aa5966e9cb78b4f93a849df99a5b250efd2",
          "asset_sha256": "eda09f8926c869c8e1a51c9966a87464b23fec963dc4c10abc9c5f7f5889298b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s02-c1-66661702d0cd",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "EventBridge sends the event to Lambda. A new environment initializes before it invokes your handler. A later event can reuse that environment, but don't write code that depends on it being there.",
          "text_sha256": "66661702d0cd2533b4f8d8ad0e1b45705732949bba75b4871c808aff02064942",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "66661702d0cd2533b4f8d8ad0e1b45705732949bba75b4871c808aff02064942",
          "asset_sha256": "cbfaea8e44f86bbce0b092072c0aa39005b4162fe3aa00f38fae903cab554ed7"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s02-c2-6cd2cf02ccdb",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Save required state to the chosen durable store. If Lambda replaces the environment, the next invocation still has a way to retrieve the data it needs.",
          "text_sha256": "6cd2cf02ccdbec32771cf59abaa9b2ce388dcd5ac9938b24d5563cba671f91b7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6cd2cf02ccdbec32771cf59abaa9b2ce388dcd5ac9938b24d5563cba671f91b7",
          "asset_sha256": "cbfaea8e44f86bbce0b092072c0aa39005b4162fe3aa00f38fae903cab554ed7"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s03-c1-0bcc90e042f6",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A ZIP package can use a compatible managed runtime. Match your code and dependencies to that runtime and keep track of updates instead of assuming the package can run under any version.",
          "text_sha256": "0bcc90e042f684dacf0aad1c83df27d7ed8088a030b290f77606c0e5347d2c68",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0bcc90e042f684dacf0aad1c83df27d7ed8088a030b290f77606c0e5347d2c68",
          "asset_sha256": "ae29b7d495392cb8921f3d7846ad319e4eb7409410eac0ea370b4505e13c58e0"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s03-c2-4d2365ec841a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An image packages code differently, but Lambda still invokes a handler through its Runtime A P I. Use a compatible Linux image for one architecture, with the runtime interface client or equivalent implementation.",
          "text_sha256": "4d2365ec841a78980c5299f987dbe161a29b3b200229109b2c5a15d4f3158032",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "697181f83e1376db11861c75d6f6db6576f4e760648b602c3ad2e3da6cfd161d",
          "asset_sha256": "ae29b7d495392cb8921f3d7846ad319e4eb7409410eac0ea370b4505e13c58e0"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p01-andrew-exp-s03-c3-8a474cf529c4",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If the image only runs a conventional server process and does not implement that contract, consider a container service such as E C S instead. Having a container image alone does not make it a Lambda Event Function.",
          "text_sha256": "8a474cf529c4915e345bf509c8495b888575817621fd6f0112dc18cca10e5d81",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3fb0df1151d1d7638103ab8eb7b9b8a5ebcb535ecf6ab4eb03bf3dbac8e4c7fb",
          "asset_sha256": "ae29b7d495392cb8921f3d7846ad319e4eb7409410eac0ea370b4505e13c58e0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "13",
      "part": "02",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m13p02-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "5942180f8219d9e0a81741032827e472dced3e034aae46a2022ffae931f8d044",
        "2": "269e8916afa10a07d7256156343970053dde8a39eafec2c3c1b8ba54f594a42f",
        "3": "6ad5d1fdb4c1784e0ecf441c1adc0d55fb98720dd2c082b59768aa31051ebf09",
        "4": "6289f77a1e3f9fa96c51f7a3a23adb3679fc81baab40e42b421fe1a4176fc141"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s01-c1-f8a1ddc0d3d8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The handler is slow. Increase memory and Lambda also gives it more C P U, so it may finish sooner. Benchmark both duration and cost instead of assuming the lowest memory setting is the least expensive.",
          "text_sha256": "f8a1ddc0d3d8407c7049f1ab7e28b508ab26060eb2bc80f0f12c7df072b53a8c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9af15d837e49a4d40c4db2255445a43c8ff336bd9e134228b6faf28219ef52b9",
          "asset_sha256": "5942180f8219d9e0a81741032827e472dced3e034aae46a2022ffae931f8d044"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s01-c2-63a42b33cff1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the function needs more room for a temporary file, configure its temporary storage separately. A larger temporary directory doesn't give the function more C P U, and it isn't a durable data store.",
          "text_sha256": "63a42b33cff17ab70ba0a611c07b07d0353fc56784083bc57832b5afbbd6a166",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "28826ebff2eb5a3b9fa82167687592b5ac3a5e9442c471d60672c12f3d1b25b2",
          "asset_sha256": "5942180f8219d9e0a81741032827e472dced3e034aae46a2022ffae931f8d044"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s01-c3-9bc2c7369aca",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Eligible on-demand Lambda Event Functions can run up to eighteen hundred seconds, or thirty minutes. That is the function's limit. A caller or integration may stop waiting sooner, so verify both before designing a long request.",
          "text_sha256": "9bc2c7369aca6a809fbd8e5cea4d1e6bcb9ba7975425952054eef10a3eecb095",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9bc2c7369aca6a809fbd8e5cea4d1e6bcb9ba7975425952054eef10a3eecb095",
          "asset_sha256": "5942180f8219d9e0a81741032827e472dced3e034aae46a2022ffae931f8d044"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s02-c1-01cc927e2763",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "First check the deployment artifact: direct ZIP upload, extracted package plus layers, and a compatible container image use different size limits. Passing the package limit does not say anything about how large an invocation may be.",
          "text_sha256": "01cc927e27635bcbc11986206e420e26fd252142763b8beeec9a4f32ca4c0610",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "01cc927e27635bcbc11986206e420e26fd252142763b8beeec9a4f32ca4c0610",
          "asset_sha256": "269e8916afa10a07d7256156343970053dde8a39eafec2c3c1b8ba54f594a42f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s02-c2-5ce1064c1703",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For the buffered synchronous path, check the six-megabyte limit each way. An asynchronous event has a one-megabyte limit. Streamed responses have a separate contract, as can the integration in front of Lambda.",
          "text_sha256": "5ce1064c1703c222c064ac234e2b51f15222bf1b3b57f98eb405b35c8e717bba",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5ce1064c1703c222c064ac234e2b51f15222bf1b3b57f98eb405b35c8e717bba",
          "asset_sha256": "269e8916afa10a07d7256156343970053dde8a39eafec2c3c1b8ba54f594a42f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s02-c3-2d60129cb3d1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If the payload is a large file, put it in S three and pass a small, authorized object reference to the function. Then test access and the full request path through any front door.",
          "text_sha256": "2d60129cb3d16a120b47a638d3489f6c061c98781b5361f2292d559049acb401",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "80aa84d689309bdc16a3fe9657422a6f29ad16d320e5d422d055f8d41607a9e1",
          "asset_sha256": "269e8916afa10a07d7256156343970053dde8a39eafec2c3c1b8ba54f594a42f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s03-c1-79d83c9604ce",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "More concurrent invocations can hit the database with more simultaneous connections. A reserved concurrency setting both allocates a share of regional capacity and caps this function. Choose the cap with the actual dependency in mind.",
          "text_sha256": "79d83c9604ce910f695629ae3973044545d3e7c69165a76333efcff3c81e7127",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "79d83c9604ce910f695629ae3973044545d3e7c69165a76333efcff3c81e7127",
          "asset_sha256": "6ad5d1fdb4c1784e0ecf441c1adc0d55fb98720dd2c082b59768aa31051ebf09"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s03-c2-e83bcbdcae17",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "At two hundred requests per second and half a second each, steady demand is about a hundred concurrent executions. That estimate gives you somewhere to start. Validate real bursts, durations, throttles and downstream load.",
          "text_sha256": "e83bcbdcae1712b0be8d590f92c3d9d2e5d907e716f885b99ced87a52ed282e4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e83bcbdcae1712b0be8d590f92c3d9d2e5d907e716f885b99ced87a52ed282e4",
          "asset_sha256": "6ad5d1fdb4c1784e0ecf441c1adc0d55fb98720dd2c082b59768aa31051ebf09"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s04-c1-6accfb0d03c4",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Reserved concurrency protects a share of capacity and limits how much the function can use. It does not prewarm an environment.",
          "text_sha256": "6accfb0d03c412ba3b2ccbc763b0ff32928e17933b89661f41adc5a33b74bc48",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6accfb0d03c412ba3b2ccbc763b0ff32928e17933b89661f41adc5a33b74bc48",
          "asset_sha256": "6289f77a1e3f9fa96c51f7a3a23adb3679fc81baab40e42b421fe1a4176fc141"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s04-c2-87a75e79f686",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Provisioned concurrency maintains pre-initialized environments on a version or alias. It can help predictable latency when requests fit the configured capacity. Allow for cost and the behavior above that capacity.",
          "text_sha256": "87a75e79f686b1376e8a4bcb40f8e523512e16d7ff2b52192f80b44c054b10af",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "87a75e79f686b1376e8a4bcb40f8e523512e16d7ff2b52192f80b44c054b10af",
          "asset_sha256": "6289f77a1e3f9fa96c51f7a3a23adb3679fc81baab40e42b421fe1a4176fc141"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p02-andrew-exp-s04-c3-c41fec9d7ab6",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "SnapStart instead restores a snapshot of an initialized environment for supported configurations. Check what your runtime supports and whether any state must be regenerated after restore. It cannot be combined with provisioned concurrency on the same version.",
          "text_sha256": "c41fec9d7ab6478c6d1e1863d3f0a7a2b20bfb2a2f49caf31d51503d67b6e042",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c41fec9d7ab6478c6d1e1863d3f0a7a2b20bfb2a2f49caf31d51503d67b6e042",
          "asset_sha256": "6289f77a1e3f9fa96c51f7a3a23adb3679fc81baab40e42b421fe1a4176fc141"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "13",
      "part": "03",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m13p03-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "1589aae25a610fa94400f73f0b3bb956f9907dde60aa71febd06db05575b6a3f",
        "2": "0bd35b24883d2cf007d07ae81ae48db4a7253157e9fbb465074a00327e62a98d"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s01-c1-80739011c8a4",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A new release should not replace all production traffic at once. Publish immutable versions so the team knows which code and configuration each version represents.",
          "text_sha256": "80739011c8a4300e19fe2ebb4337dde0939dd1ee35b1686427eab2d21eb71a3a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "80739011c8a4300e19fe2ebb4337dde0939dd1ee35b1686427eab2d21eb71a3a",
          "asset_sha256": "1589aae25a610fa94400f73f0b3bb956f9907dde60aa71febd06db05575b6a3f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s01-c2-00a69a06097c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Keep callers on the stable production alias and route a small share to the new version. Here the new version receives ten percent. Watch its results before increasing that share.",
          "text_sha256": "00a69a06097c7775329e88d941ea49a255619dc1c033a3898e8f2d89b234e1db",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "00a69a06097c7775329e88d941ea49a255619dc1c033a3898e8f2d89b234e1db",
          "asset_sha256": "1589aae25a610fa94400f73f0b3bb956f9907dde60aa71febd06db05575b6a3f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s01-c3-fa6c72432964",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use deployment hooks and alarms to catch unhealthy behavior and roll traffic back. An alias rollback does not undo database changes the new code already made. Validate those changes separately.",
          "text_sha256": "fa6c72432964ca405fb3ed9e7c77f319bb23c15f8bde4c478050d32b6507ecc4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fa6c72432964ca405fb3ed9e7c77f319bb23c15f8bde4c478050d32b6507ecc4",
          "asset_sha256": "1589aae25a610fa94400f73f0b3bb956f9907dde60aa71febd06db05575b6a3f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s02-c1-7b372ccd6a2b",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "An invocation failed. Start with its request I D and the relevant error in CloudWatch Logs. Keep logs structured and leave secrets out of them.",
          "text_sha256": "7b372ccd6a2b48146dbdd5efb102e0adc24fa167f62bfa4747f46f2510feabcf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9288f8f30f7436cf78e5d0c35000dd77713c34f192235b7e1a9bf10b06ea3da3",
          "asset_sha256": "0bd35b24883d2cf007d07ae81ae48db4a7253157e9fbb465074a00327e62a98d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s02-c2-e11fdd0dff24",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now ask whether the failure is isolated or part of a trend. Compare invocations, errors, duration and throttles. That can distinguish one bad input from a broad capacity problem.",
          "text_sha256": "e11fdd0dff2439a8c44e0a79d1372e445108225fda41d64f9e871649eefc9cf4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e11fdd0dff2439a8c44e0a79d1372e445108225fda41d64f9e871649eefc9cf4",
          "asset_sha256": "0bd35b24883d2cf007d07ae81ae48db4a7253157e9fbb465074a00327e62a98d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m13p03-andrew-exp-s02-c3-3011e7451c26",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "When the request calls another service, a trace can show where time was spent. Configure the supported instrumentation and permissions, then tie that trace to the same request instead of guessing from total duration.",
          "text_sha256": "3011e7451c26ce5c752f2b90e48ac12c77b03805746628511cdcedc6dabe0c9e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3011e7451c26ce5c752f2b90e48ac12c77b03805746628511cdcedc6dabe0c9e",
          "asset_sha256": "0bd35b24883d2cf007d07ae81ae48db4a7253157e9fbb465074a00327e62a98d"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
